// conn_shadow_local.cla: TestConnShadowedLocalIsNil's own fixture (Task 4,
// binary-files phase -- flipped from the old TestConnShadowedLocalRejected
// pin now that `connection` is an ordinary value, ir.cla). A local `var
// conn: connection` SHADOWS the global `conn` of the same name; the
// method call below resolves to the LOCAL (lowIsLocal/lowExpr, not
// lowConnSlotOf's name map -- that map is name-keyed and would otherwise
// misresolve this to the global's slot, final-review Important 2's
// original bug). The local is never assigned, so it's `nil` (0) by
// construction -- `conn.send("shadowed")` on it is a legal BUILD (a local
// connection receiver is no longer rejected) but a runtime panic (`use of
// nil connection`, runtime/clarus/conn.cla's h == 0 check), never a
// silent reuse of the global's own open slot.
var conn: connection

on App.startCLI(args: list of string) {
    conn.open(serial "modem:9600")
    useLocal()
}

// useLocal must stay reachable from a real entry point -- shake.cla's
// whole-program reachability pass over the IR arena strips any function
// never called, and a dead useLocal would never exercise lowConnMethod at
// all (a silent false-pass for this fixture, not a real regression pin).
func useLocal() {
    var conn: connection
    conn.send("shadowed")
}
